Relevant columns and why we need them  
• `fullVisitorId` : identifies each customer so we can follow what else they bought.  
• `_TABLE_SUFFIX` : pseudo‑column that lets us keep only July‑2017 daily tables (`LIKE '201707%'`).  
• `hits` (repeated) → `item` (repeated) →  
 • `item.productName` : name of every product that was purchased.  
 • `item.itemQuantity` : how many units of each product were bought (to count “sales”).  
 • `item.itemRevenue` : revenue per product (alternative measure).  

Typical filter / join conditions  
• `_TABLE_SUFFIX LIKE '201707%'` → restrict to July 2017.  
• `LOWER(item.productName) = LOWER('youtube men’s vintage henley')` (or `LIKE '%vintage%henley%'`) → sessions where the target product was bought.  
• `item.productName <> 'Youtube Men’s Vintage Henley'` → remove the target product when we look for “other” items.  

Below are ten exploratory → analytical queries (all return at most 20 rows) that gradually build up to the final answer.  
Use the project / dataset / table exactly as shown.

```sql
-- 1. Peek at all July‑2017 product names that contain “henley”
SELECT DISTINCT item.productName
FROM `bigquery-public-data.google_analytics_sample.ga_sessions_*` AS s,
     UNNEST(s.hits)           AS h,
     UNNEST(h.item)           AS item
WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX LIKE '201707%'
  AND LOWER(item.productName) LIKE '%henley%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Show customers (visitors) that bought the Henley in July‑2017
SELECT DISTINCT s.fullVisitorId
FROM `bigquery-public-data.google_analytics_sample.ga_sessions_*` AS s,
     UNNEST(s.hits) AS h,
     UNNEST(h.item) AS item
WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX LIKE '201707%'
  AND LOWER(item.productName) = LOWER('youtube men’s vintage henley')
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. List every item those customers purchased (including the Henley)
SELECT DISTINCT s.fullVisitorId, item.productName
FROM `bigquery-public-data.google_analytics_sample.ga_sessions_*` AS s,
     UNNEST(s.hits) AS h,
     UNNEST(h.item) AS item
WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX LIKE '201707%'
  AND s.fullVisitorId IN (
        SELECT DISTINCT fullVisitorId
        FROM `bigquery-public-data.google_analytics_sample.ga_sessions_*`,
             UNNEST(hits) AS h2,
             UNNEST(h2.item) AS it2
        WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX LIKE '201707%'
          AND LOWER(it2.productName)=LOWER('youtube men’s vintage henley')
      )
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Same as #3 but exclude the Henley itself
SELECT DISTINCT s.fullVisitorId, item.productName
FROM `bigquery-public-data.google_analytics_sample.ga_sessions_*` AS s,
     UNNEST(s.hits) AS h,
     UNNEST(h.item) AS item
WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX LIKE '201707%'
  AND s.fullVisitorId IN (
        SELECT DISTINCT fullVisitorId
        FROM `bigquery-public-data.google_analytics_sample.ga_sessions_*`,
             UNNEST(hits) AS h2,
             UNNEST(h2.item) AS it2
        WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX LIKE '201707%'
          AND LOWER(it2.productName)=LOWER('youtube men’s vintage henley')
      )
  AND LOWER(item.productName) <> LOWER('youtube men’s vintage henley')
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Count how many times each “other” product was bought by those customers
SELECT item.productName,
       SUM(item.itemQuantity) AS total_units
FROM `bigquery-public-data.google_analytics_sample.ga_sessions_*` AS s,
     UNNEST(s.hits) AS h,
     UNNEST(h.item) AS item
WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX LIKE '201707%'
  AND s.fullVisitorId IN (
        SELECT DISTINCT fullVisitorId
        FROM `bigquery-public-data.google_analytics_sample.ga_sessions_*`,
             UNNEST(hits) AS h2,
             UNNEST(h2.item) AS it2
        WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX LIKE '201707%'
          AND LOWER(it2.productName)=LOWER('youtube men’s vintage henley')
      )
  AND LOWER(item.productName) <> LOWER('youtube men’s vintage henley')
GROUP BY item.productName
ORDER BY total_units DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Same as #5 but ranking by revenue instead of quantity
SELECT item.productName,
       SUM(item.itemRevenue)/1e6 AS revenue_usd
FROM `bigquery-public-data.google_analytics_sample.ga_sessions_*` AS s,
     UNNEST(s.hits) AS h,
     UNNEST(h.item) AS item
WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX LIKE '201707%'
  AND s.fullVisitorId IN (
        SELECT DISTINCT fullVisitorId
        FROM `bigquery-public-data.google_analytics_sample.ga_sessions_*`,
             UNNEST(hits) AS h2,
             UNNEST(h2.item) AS it2
        WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX LIKE '201707%'
          AND LOWER(it2.productName)=LOWER('youtube men’s vintage henley')
      )
  AND LOWER(item.productName) <> LOWER('youtube men’s vintage henley')
GROUP BY item.productName
ORDER BY revenue_usd DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Put both quantity and revenue together for the “other” products
SELECT item.productName,
       SUM(item.itemQuantity)                AS total_units,
       SUM(item.itemRevenue)/1e6             AS revenue_usd
FROM `bigquery-public-data.google_analytics_sample.ga_sessions_*` AS s,
     UNNEST(s.hits) AS h,
     UNNEST(h.item) AS item
WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX LIKE '201707%'
  AND s.fullVisitorId IN (
        SELECT DISTINCT fullVisitorId
        FROM `bigquery-public-data.google_analytics_sample.ga_sessions_*`,
             UNNEST(hits) AS h2,
             UNNEST(h2.item) AS it2
        WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX LIKE '201707%'
          AND LOWER(it2.productName)=LOWER('youtube men’s vintage henley')
      )
  AND LOWER(item.productName) <> LOWER('youtube men’s vintage henley')
GROUP BY item.productName
ORDER BY total_units DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Use a CTE for clarity and return top 5 products by units
WITH henley_buyers AS (
  SELECT DISTINCT fullVisitorId
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.google_analytics_sample.ga_sessions_*`,
       UNNEST(hits) AS h,
       UNNEST(h.item) AS itm
  WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX LIKE '201707%'
    AND LOWER(itm.productName)=LOWER('youtube men’s vintage henley')
)
SELECT it.productName,
       SUM(it.itemQuantity) AS units
FROM `bigquery-public-data.google_analytics_sample.ga_sessions_*` AS s,
     UNNEST(s.hits) AS h,
     UNNEST(h.item) AS it
WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX LIKE '201707%'
  AND s.fullVisitorId IN (SELECT fullVisitorId FROM henley_buyers)
  AND LOWER(it.productName) <> LOWER('youtube men’s vintage henley')
GROUP BY it.productName
ORDER BY units DESC
LIMIT 5;
```

```sql
-- 9. Same CTE but take only the single top‑selling product (units); show tie‑breaking by revenue
WITH henley_buyers AS (
  SELECT DISTINCT fullVisitorId
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.google_analytics_sample.ga_sessions_*`,
       UNNEST(hits) AS h,
       UNNEST(h.item) AS itm
  WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX LIKE '201707%'
    AND LOWER(itm.productName)=LOWER('youtube men’s vintage henley')
),
other_sales AS (
  SELECT it.productName,
         SUM(it.itemQuantity) AS units,
         SUM(it.itemRevenue)  AS revenue
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.google_analytics_sample.ga_sessions_*` AS s,
       UNNEST(s.hits) AS h,
       UNNEST(h.item) AS it
  WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX LIKE '201707%'
    AND s.fullVisitorId IN (SELECT fullVisitorId FROM henley_buyers)
    AND LOWER(it.productName) <> LOWER('youtube men’s vintage henley')
  GROUP BY it.productName
)
SELECT *
FROM other_sales
ORDER BY units DESC, revenue DESC
LIMIT 1;
```

```sql
-- 10. FINAL ANSWER QUERY – returns the single top‑selling (by units) product bought
--      by July‑2017 customers who purchased “Youtube Men’s Vintage Henley”,
--      excluding the Henley itself.
WITH henley_buyers AS (
  SELECT DISTINCT fullVisitorId
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.google_analytics_sample.ga_sessions_*`,
       UNNEST(hits) AS hit,
       UNNEST(hit.item) AS it
  WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX LIKE '201707%'
    AND LOWER(it.productName)=LOWER('youtube men’s vintage henley')
),
other_items AS (
  SELECT it.productName,
         SUM(it.itemQuantity) AS total_units
  FROM `bigquery-public-data.google_analytics_sample.ga_sessions_*` AS s,
       UNNEST(s.hits) AS hit,
       UNNEST(hit.item) AS it
  WHERE _TABLE_SUFFIX LIKE '201707%'
    AND s.fullVisitorId IN (SELECT fullVisitorId FROM henley_buyers)
    AND LOWER(it.productName) <> LOWER('youtube men’s vintage henley')
  GROUP BY it.productName
)
SELECT productName       AS top_selling_product,
       total_units       AS units_sold_to_those_customers
FROM other_items
ORDER BY total_units DESC
LIMIT 1;
```

